Now define a new equation that treats time as an active field rather than a passive parameter.

Time field: ( \Theta(x^\mu) ) (a scalar or multi-component field)

Dynamics of time: [ \mathcal{E}\Theta: \quad F\big(\Theta, \partial\mu \Theta, g_{\mu\nu}, \text{matter fields}\big) = 0 ] This says: geometry, matter, and “time texture” co-evolve. Local dilation, compression, branching, etc., are encoded in (\Theta).

You can then define experienced time for an observer worldline (\gamma): [ \mathcal{T}\text{obs}[\gamma] = \int\gamma \Phi\big(\Theta, g_{\mu\nu}, u^\mu\big), d\lambda ] where (\Phi) is your “experience kernel”.

